# Words in `Rat(U)`

[JZLA20, §4.2] constructs `Rat(U) = ℕ[U ♮ X] \ {0}` from the `U`-biset `U ♮ X` of *words* in the
`U`-biset `X` of formal rational operations.  The elements of `U ♮ X` are the *words*: finite
sequences of elements of `X` (modulo the `U`-biset relations, which for the model `RatU U` of
`Rat/RTerm.lean` are realised by the action axioms of the rational semiring structure).

For the induction of [JZLA20, Proposition 5.1] the two facts about words that matter are:

* **every element of `Rat(U)` is a finite sum of words** (`RatU.IsWord.sum_decomp`), so that an
  element can be split either as a `⋄`-operation, or as a non-trivial product of words, or as a
  non-trivial sum — the four-way case distinction of the proof of Proposition 5.1;
* **a word has width one** (`RatU.IsWord.wid_tree`), i.e. `Tree α` is a single root extension,
  which is [JZLA20, Lemma 4.3(xiii)] and is what makes the "equality" case of the induction give
  a single coefficient.

In the term model `RatU U` a word is generated by: the image `ofGroup u` of a group element, the
product of two words, and the `⋄` of an arbitrary element (in the model `ℕ[U ♮ X]`, the elements
of `X` are precisely the `s⋄`, `s ∈ ℕ[U ♮ X]`) — this last clause is formalised with no
hypothesis on `s`, since `RatU U` has a total `⋄` and the extra elements `s⋄` with `s = 0` are
words of width one as well.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.Rat.OfGroup
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.Tree.Log

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Work.ORHughesFree

namespace RatU

variable {U : Type} [Group U]

/-- **A word of `Rat(U)`**: an element of the `U`-biset `U ♮ X` of [JZLA20, §4.2] — generated by
the images of the group elements, by products, and by the rational operation `⋄`.

The `⋄`-clause carries the hypothesis `x ≠ 0`: in the paper `X` consists of one letter `s⋄` for
each *non-zero* `s ∈ ℕ[U ♮ X]`, and accordingly the letters here are the `x⋄` with `x ≠ 0`.  (The
naive total clause `IsWord (s⋄)` for *all* `s` would make `IsWord 0` true, since `0⋄ = 0`,
contradicting `isWord_ne_zero`.) -/
inductive IsWord : RatU U → Prop
  /-- the image of a group element -/
  | ofGroup (u : U) : IsWord (ofGroup u)
  /-- the product of two words -/
  | mul {x y : RatU U} (hx : IsWord x) (hy : IsWord y) : IsWord (x * y)
  /-- the `⋄` of a non-zero element (the elements of `X` are the `s⋄`, `s ≠ 0`) -/
  | rat (x : RatU U) (hx : x ≠ 0) : IsWord (RatU.rational.ratOp x)

end RatU

end Work.ORHughesFree
